Follow the rules in `.claude/software-factory.md`. It is the single copy shared with Claude Code.

In short:

- `.software-factory/project.json` holds the `project_id`. Pass it to every `software-factory` MCP tool call.
- Never assume the stack, architecture or contracts. Read them with `get_implementation_context`, `read_backlog` and `read_artifact`.
- Work is planned in the factory. Implement one execution-plan task at a time (see `02-implement-task`). Don't break work down yourself.
- For questions about existing code, use the code-graph tools (see `04-code-context`) before opening files.
- If the MCP server isn't connected, say so and point to `INTEGRATION.md`. Don't guess the specification.
